DIM SHARED DLINE(1 TO 600) AS STRING, DLINE_N AS INTEGER

' --- turn machinery (ENGINE, by design) ---
' Turn STRUCTURE is engine: how many steps remain, whose turn it is, whether a roll is
' owed. What a turn COSTS and what combat does with it are game rules. Today only game/
' and dungeon.bas fill these, so the ENGINE.BI hoarding audit would flag them as unused --
' they are RESERVED there on purpose, because the deeper tactical-combat screen in
' plans/PLANS.todo needs engine-side initiative + turn order and will consume them.
' See the allowlist in tests/audit-boundary.sh.
DIM SHARED AS INTEGER turn_num, steps_left, need_roll
DIM SHARED c AS CURSOR
DIM SHARED bnr_l2 AS STRING, bnr_bx1 AS INTEGER, bnr_bx2 AS INTEGER   ' last Banner's prompt line + box, for the keypress flash

' --- dice display state + DPoly polyhedron fonts ---
DIM SHARED die_a AS INTEGER, die_b AS INTEGER    ' last dice shown by RollDiceShow
' PER-DIE FACES of the last animated roll, published by EVERY renderer (pips, font polyhedra and
' the 3D dice alike). The roll helpers return a TOTAL, which is all most callers want -- but a
' roll where the dice mean DIFFERENT THINGS needs them apart. Combat initiative is the case: two
' d20s thrown together, one the player's and one the monster's, so the two sides are settled by
' the same throw the player watches rather than by a visible roll and a silent one.
' DIE_FACE_N = 0 means the last roll published nothing (Real Dice: the player rolled physically,
' so there are no faces to read).
DIM SHARED DIE_FACE(1 TO 12) AS INTEGER, DIE_FACE_N AS INTEGER

' --- HELD DICE: a PARTIAL re-roll ------------------------------------------------
' The counterpart to DIE_FACE. That one reads the dice apart; this one re-throws only some of
' them, leaving the rest lying where they are, showing what they showed.
'
' It exists because "3d6, re-roll 1s and 2s" is a rule about INDIVIDUAL dice, and rolling only
' the chosen dice in a fresh tray shows the wrong thing: the kept dice vanish and the player can
' no longer see the rule being applied. On a table you pick up the dice you are re-throwing and
' leave the others.
'
' Set holds, then roll the FULL set as normal -- the held indices simply do not tumble:
'     RollHoldClear : RollHoldSet 1, 4 : RollHoldSet 3, 6 : v = AnimatedRoll%(3, 6, 0, "...")
' Consumed and cleared by that roll. A renderer with no hold support ignores them and re-rolls
' everything, which is wrong-looking but never wrong-VALUED -- the caller reads DIE_FACE either way.
DIM SHARED ROLLHOLD(1 TO 12) AS INTEGER          ' per die index: pinned face (0 = free to roll)
DIM SHARED ROLLHOLD_ON AS INTEGER                ' any holds pending

' --- ROLL SEQUENCE: several passes sharing ONE tray -------------------------------
' A multi-pass roll (3d6 re-rolling its 1s and 2s) is several calls into the roller, and each
' call used to photograph the screen, draw its tray, and put the photograph BACK -- so the tray
' and every die on it vanished between passes and were rebuilt from nothing. Even with the held
' dice pinned to the same seats, the box blinking out and back reads as the dice being thrown
' around: what you see is not "one die was picked up", it is "everything went away and returned".
'
' Between RollSeqBegin and RollSeqEnd the snapshot is taken ONCE and restored ONCE, so the tray
' stays put for the whole sequence and only the dice inside it change.
' Where the last roll's dice could reach, and where its running-total lane starts (canvas px).
' The lane is printed immediately under the tray and a die is drawn centred on its position, so a
' die resting on the box floor hangs BELOW it -- the two are one bad constant away from colliding,
' and the collision is text with dice drawn over it. Published so a dev check can assert the gap
' instead of it being re-discovered by eye every time the tray or the die size moves.
DIM SHARED roll_floor_y AS INTEGER               ' lowest pixel a settled die can occupy
DIM SHARED roll_sum_y AS INTEGER                 ' top of the running-total lane
DIM SHARED roll_tray_bot AS INTEGER              ' bottom edge of the drawn tray rectangle
DIM SHARED rollseq_on AS INTEGER                 ' -1 while consecutive rolls share a tray
DIM SHARED rollseq_snap AS LONG                  ' the screen underneath that shared tray
' DPoly polyhedron die fonts, indexed BY SIDE COUNT: DFONT(20) is the d20 font.
' Loaded from assets/fonts/dpoly by InitDice; 0 = failed to load (falls back to
' the number tumbler). Each glyph IS a die face: 'A'+n draws the solid variant,
' 'a'+n the outline variant -- see DieGlyphCode / DrawFontDie.
DIM SHARED DFONT(1 TO 20) AS LONG
DIM SHARED DFROT AS LONG                          ' scratch image a die renders into, then rotate-blits (tumble spin)
CONST DFROT_W = 160, DFROT_H = 200               ' scratch size (fits a d20 @56pt + headroom for the top vertex)
DIM SHARED last_raw AS INTEGER                    ' last natural dice sum (before modifiers) from DoRoll

